1
00:02:30,967 --> 00:02:37,487
This is the time known as the Great Pirate Era.

2
00:02:37,787 --> 00:02:41,807
A countless array of pirates go to battle across the seas in search of the One Piece,

3
00:02:42,047 --> 00:02:46,007
the legendary treasure left behind by Gold Roger, King of the Pirates.

4
00:02:46,487 --> 00:02:50,867
Maki D. Luffy, a boy whose body turned to rubber after eating the gum-gum fruit,

5
00:02:51,167 --> 00:02:53,627
set sail to become the next King of the Pirates.

6
00:02:54,007 --> 00:02:56,607
As Luffy and his crew conquer numerous obstacles,

7
00:02:56,907 --> 00:02:59,727
they capture the unwanted attention of the world government,

8
00:02:59,727 --> 00:03:02,787
which will use any means necessary to stop them.

9
00:03:04,147 --> 00:03:05,507
This site!

10
00:03:06,587 --> 00:03:09,367
Can't wait to see what kind of adventure's up next!

11
00:03:09,747 --> 00:03:13,147
With a charted course awash in danger and intrigue,

12
00:03:13,367 --> 00:03:17,427
the crew will come a path across the Grand Line to the New World.

13
00:03:20,767 --> 00:03:23,287
After his crew was scattered around the world,

14
00:03:23,627 --> 00:03:25,647
Luffy set off to rescue his brother Ace,

15
00:03:25,727 --> 00:03:27,067
who had been captured by the Navy

16
00:03:27,067 --> 00:03:30,327
and sent to a massive prison known as Impel Down.

17
00:03:30,947 --> 00:03:33,247
On his way down to level five,

18
00:03:33,387 --> 00:03:37,007
a closely guarded floor where the most infamous criminals were held,

19
00:03:37,547 --> 00:03:40,167
Luffy encountered an old acquaintance.

20
00:03:40,567 --> 00:03:42,067
Time for my specialty!

21
00:03:44,567 --> 00:03:45,987
Causing chaos!

22
00:03:46,867 --> 00:03:48,287
Works for me!

23
00:03:48,287 --> 00:04:02,347
Break through the crimson hell!

24
00:04:02,347 --> 00:04:04,847
Buggy's chaos-inducing plan!

25
00:04:12,047 --> 00:04:13,347
Gong-gong!

26
00:04:14,147 --> 00:04:14,407
Woo!

27
00:04:14,407 --> 00:04:25,187
I'm just screwing with you.

28
00:04:25,847 --> 00:04:28,507
I call this my chop-chop emergency escape!

29
00:04:28,507 --> 00:04:45,087
A chop like that should break your skull just fine!

30
00:04:45,447 --> 00:04:48,727
And this one here is my aerial tailspin, ding-tong!

31
00:04:51,227 --> 00:04:54,127
You picked the wrong clown to mess with, monkey!

32
00:04:54,127 --> 00:04:54,727
Don't go, monkey!

33
00:04:59,727 --> 00:05:00,227
No!

34
00:05:03,787 --> 00:05:05,167
Hey, hey, don't touch it!

35
00:05:11,167 --> 00:05:11,607
No!

36
00:05:11,607 --> 00:05:28,727
Damn, you got a lot stronger, didn't you, kid?

37
00:05:29,147 --> 00:05:31,567
I don't know. These guys are pretty tough. Where are they?

38
00:05:31,567 --> 00:05:35,107
Sea monkeys. Blue Gorillas, they're called. Or Blue Gordy for short.

39
00:05:35,347 --> 00:05:38,567
But stay sharp. Should be four more of them left to take the place...

40
00:05:38,567 --> 00:05:41,047
Well, never mind. Guess you got them already.

41
00:05:42,287 --> 00:05:46,227
Either way, I hope that's the last of them. I don't have time to mess around right now.

42
00:05:46,867 --> 00:05:49,227
That guy's a monster. How did he do that?

43
00:05:49,327 --> 00:05:50,947
You came here to let us out, didn't you?

44
00:05:51,067 --> 00:05:53,267
We'll be your best friend, pal. I promise.

45
00:05:57,447 --> 00:05:58,287
Something wrong?

46
00:05:58,287 --> 00:06:01,947
You bet there is. I thought you said only one prisoner escaped.

47
00:06:02,487 --> 00:06:04,127
Yeah, it was just the clown guy.

48
00:06:04,827 --> 00:06:07,467
Pretty sure I saw two guys, but maybe I'm crazy.

49
00:06:07,467 --> 00:06:12,987
And speaking of crazy, five Blue Gorillas got taken down in front of community cell number ten.

50
00:06:12,987 --> 00:06:15,087
On level one? There's no way.

51
00:06:15,087 --> 00:06:19,087
The prisoners down there aren't strong enough to take on even one Blue Gorillas.

52
00:06:19,087 --> 00:06:25,007
What? You broke in here to rescue Ace?

53
00:06:25,187 --> 00:06:25,587
Yep.

54
00:06:27,207 --> 00:06:29,347
Shh. We gotta stay quiet.

55
00:06:29,467 --> 00:06:31,307
I'm not really following your own advice there.

56
00:06:31,427 --> 00:06:33,907
We could well use the keys to our cell if you're not too busy.

57
00:06:34,107 --> 00:06:36,507
Would you shut the hell up? Nobody gives a damn.

58
00:06:36,727 --> 00:06:38,067
Wait, do you know Ace?

59
00:06:38,067 --> 00:06:39,067
Yeah.

60
00:06:40,447 --> 00:06:43,887
And though I can see the resemblance, he made a better impression than you did.

61
00:06:43,887 --> 00:07:02,567
You really think this is the time to throw a party?

62
00:07:02,887 --> 00:07:08,087
How can you plan on beating Luffy and the rest of his crew when you don't have any idea where they are?

63
00:07:08,087 --> 00:07:10,767
Oh, come on. Don't be such a party, Pooper Alvita.

64
00:07:10,767 --> 00:07:13,827
We'll find Luffy when we find him, so just calm down.

65
00:07:15,147 --> 00:07:18,267
If you're looking for Luffy, I can tell you where he is.

66
00:07:18,667 --> 00:07:20,307
There you go. Problem solved.

67
00:07:20,427 --> 00:07:23,107
This fellow here can lead us straight to straw hat any time.

68
00:07:23,587 --> 00:07:25,327
Hold on. Who in the hell are you?

69
00:07:26,247 --> 00:07:28,507
Oh, hello. Sorry for crashing your party.

70
00:07:29,987 --> 00:07:34,627
Anyway, the name's Ace, and as you might guess, I was drawn here by the delicious aroma of your feast.

71
00:07:34,887 --> 00:07:35,847
Thanks for feeding me.

72
00:07:36,207 --> 00:07:38,627
No need to be polite. We're all friends here.

73
00:07:38,627 --> 00:07:40,707
It's a pleasure to make your acquaintance, friend.

74
00:07:41,287 --> 00:07:44,267
Just because you introduce yourself doesn't mean you get to eat my food.

75
00:07:44,447 --> 00:07:46,327
My ship, my banquet, my rules.

76
00:07:46,527 --> 00:07:48,047
So take that meat out of your mouth.

77
00:07:48,287 --> 00:07:51,467
Captain, be careful. That guy is fire fisting.

78
00:07:51,467 --> 00:07:54,387
Just let the man eat. He's from Whitebeard's crew.

79
00:07:54,727 --> 00:07:56,067
The second division commander.

80
00:07:56,427 --> 00:07:57,867
Did you say Whitebeard?

81
00:07:57,927 --> 00:07:58,227
What?

82
00:07:58,227 --> 00:08:01,207
Oh, you guys know the old man, huh?

83
00:08:01,607 --> 00:08:03,867
That's nice. He's a real...

84
00:08:03,867 --> 00:08:05,007
He's sleeping!

85
00:08:05,007 --> 00:08:10,427
After he woke up, we had a few drinks, chatted it up, and became pretty good pals.

86
00:08:10,827 --> 00:08:13,827
So yeah, I think it sucks your brother got thrown in here too.

87
00:08:14,567 --> 00:08:16,347
Kind of stupid of the Navy to do that.

88
00:08:16,607 --> 00:08:18,187
I'm sure Whitebeard will give him hell.

89
00:08:18,267 --> 00:08:20,067
I heard they're keeping Ace on level five.

90
00:08:20,267 --> 00:08:21,887
Could you show me the way to get there?

91
00:08:22,007 --> 00:08:23,927
Not a chance in hell! Go by yourself!

92
00:08:23,927 --> 00:08:26,327
What, do you think I'm your friend now?

93
00:08:26,627 --> 00:08:29,447
In fact, you can die down here for all I care.

94
00:08:29,967 --> 00:08:30,807
So long.

95
00:08:32,307 --> 00:08:35,427
If you don't want to break out of here, I'll just do it on my own.

96
00:08:35,767 --> 00:08:38,207
Okay, but there's ten battleships out there.

97
00:08:38,387 --> 00:08:39,907
I hope you've got a good plan.

98
00:08:41,907 --> 00:08:43,127
That's not good.

99
00:08:43,587 --> 00:08:44,947
All right, I get it.

100
00:08:45,047 --> 00:08:47,427
They must be expecting an attack from Whitebeard.

101
00:08:50,407 --> 00:08:52,067
Guess I picked a bad time.

102
00:08:52,067 --> 00:08:54,987
Ah, maybe I could just lay low.

103
00:08:56,947 --> 00:08:58,587
I'll find someone else then.

104
00:08:59,387 --> 00:09:01,267
So are we getting the key or not?

105
00:09:02,887 --> 00:09:05,267
No, no, I must be imagining things.

106
00:09:05,547 --> 00:09:07,607
What would he be doing with something like that?

107
00:09:10,567 --> 00:09:11,547
Then again.

108
00:09:18,767 --> 00:09:20,327
Well, good luck with your escape.

109
00:09:20,427 --> 00:09:21,247
I gotta get moving.

110
00:09:22,067 --> 00:09:25,647
No, that's gotta be it.

111
00:09:26,267 --> 00:09:26,947
White straw!

112
00:09:26,947 --> 00:09:27,787
Go, go, go!

113
00:09:28,807 --> 00:09:29,807
What's your problem?

114
00:09:30,407 --> 00:09:31,167
Up there!

115
00:09:31,967 --> 00:09:32,587
No, no!

116
00:09:32,587 --> 00:09:35,527
No kidding, because you won't stop yelling so much!

117
00:09:35,607 --> 00:09:38,167
By the way, that's a lovely armlet you've got there, Straw Hat.

118
00:09:38,227 --> 00:09:39,867
Do you think you can give it to me pretty, please?

119
00:09:40,207 --> 00:09:41,447
No, it's a gift from Nami.

120
00:09:41,527 --> 00:09:42,547
What do you want with it?

121
00:09:42,667 --> 00:09:45,527
If you let me have the armlet, I'll show you how to get to this.

122
00:09:45,527 --> 00:09:48,207
Is that a promise?

123
00:09:48,527 --> 00:09:50,567
Sure, just fork it over, kiddo.

124
00:09:50,987 --> 00:09:52,707
Okay, you got a deal.

125
00:09:52,907 --> 00:09:54,107
All right!

126
00:09:54,907 --> 00:09:56,647
First off, let's shake those goggles.

127
00:09:57,447 --> 00:09:58,767
Grab onto my feet, okay?

128
00:09:58,987 --> 00:09:59,507
Your feet.

129
00:10:00,447 --> 00:10:01,767
Good, now start running.

130
00:10:01,767 --> 00:10:05,867
Be careful with those.

131
00:10:06,007 --> 00:10:07,327
Can't have you chop them!

132
00:10:09,327 --> 00:10:12,927
Let's review how Buggy's chop-chop power works, shall we?

133
00:10:13,387 --> 00:10:17,627
When he chop-chops his body to pieces, he can control each part however he likes,

134
00:10:17,767 --> 00:10:19,647
but only within a limited area.

135
00:10:19,647 --> 00:10:25,027
And if his feet aren't close to the ground, he becomes unable to levitate the rest of his body.

136
00:10:28,027 --> 00:10:30,607
Damn, I am one lucky clown!

137
00:10:33,407 --> 00:10:37,927
I got the treasure of a lifetime, and to take it out of this crap hole in one shot!

138
00:10:46,927 --> 00:10:47,407
Captain!

139
00:10:48,467 --> 00:10:48,887
Captain!

140
00:10:49,647 --> 00:10:52,127
What?

141
00:10:53,867 --> 00:10:56,887
I'm just starting to have second thoughts about this place, that's all.

142
00:10:57,567 --> 00:11:00,367
You sure this is the cave where Captain John kept his hidden treasure,

143
00:11:00,607 --> 00:11:03,087
and the crew he left behind never found it this whole time?

144
00:11:03,267 --> 00:11:04,707
It seems a bit too easy.

145
00:11:05,427 --> 00:11:07,447
Just hold the lantern and keep walking.

146
00:11:07,727 --> 00:11:08,167
Yes, sir.

147
00:11:10,747 --> 00:11:12,107
Now look alive, boys.

148
00:11:12,187 --> 00:11:14,747
The treasure is near, but so is unspeakable danger.

149
00:11:15,087 --> 00:11:18,747
If you let your guard down, even for a second, then death will creep up on you.

150
00:11:18,747 --> 00:11:24,787
There's no telling what kind of monsters will appear, or what vicious booby traps await to kill us all.

151
00:11:24,787 --> 00:11:30,907
Come on, men. Another fine day carving out tunnels awaits us.

152
00:11:30,907 --> 00:11:32,027
Right-o, boss!

153
00:11:32,027 --> 00:11:34,267
Oh, you three must be the new guys.

154
00:11:34,267 --> 00:11:41,507
Nothing like working up a sweat, right, boss? All a man really needs is a pickaxe in his hand and a tunnel to dig.

155
00:11:41,507 --> 00:11:46,747
That's right, and because of our good old-fashioned elbow grease, everyone who comes to this tunnel will smile.

156
00:11:46,747 --> 00:11:47,587
It's liberating!

157
00:11:47,587 --> 00:11:51,507
You know, after all this hard labor, we ought to hit it with the old bilge barge for a-

158
00:11:51,507 --> 00:11:51,787
Ah!

159
00:11:52,787 --> 00:11:55,787
How dare you make me work like one of your lackeys!

160
00:11:57,207 --> 00:12:00,827
Unfortunately, that wasn't the first dead end we hit, and it wouldn't be the last.

161
00:12:01,147 --> 00:12:03,827
We ran all over the Grand Line looking for that treasure.

162
00:12:03,827 --> 00:12:13,307
As if that wasn't crappy enough, my ill-fated treasure hunts brought me straight to a navy post one day, and the bastards threw me in this dump when they captured me.

163
00:12:15,147 --> 00:12:19,827
But maybe it was destiny all along, guiding me to Captain John's treasure.

164
00:12:20,347 --> 00:12:21,267
Step on it, strong.

165
00:12:21,387 --> 00:12:22,547
Hard time to waste it.

166
00:12:23,307 --> 00:12:25,847
Follow me, and we'll be at level two in no time.

167
00:12:26,447 --> 00:12:28,467
Level two? Were you listening to me?

168
00:12:28,467 --> 00:12:30,747
I said I wanted to go to level five!

169
00:12:30,927 --> 00:12:32,807
Ah, don't you know how numbers work?

170
00:12:32,987 --> 00:12:35,207
You gotta go through two to get to five!

171
00:12:35,307 --> 00:12:36,107
Let me explain.

172
00:12:36,327 --> 00:12:38,147
Think of this as an upside-down tower.

173
00:12:38,507 --> 00:12:42,447
The place we're in right now is called level one, which is the first basement floor.

174
00:12:42,727 --> 00:12:45,387
After that, you go to level two and level three and so on.

175
00:12:45,527 --> 00:12:48,307
The deeper you get, the more infamous the criminals are.

176
00:12:49,507 --> 00:12:54,347
They tortured me in the fires of level four a few times, but that's as far as I've gone myself.

177
00:12:54,647 --> 00:12:57,147
Everything else is just things I've heard from other people.

178
00:12:57,147 --> 00:13:00,247
Level five is where they take all the big shots, though.

179
00:13:00,447 --> 00:13:03,427
So in a bounty as high as your brother's, he's gotta be there.

180
00:13:07,867 --> 00:13:12,527
As for what's below level five, well, I've heard some rumors, but the details are scarce.

181
00:13:12,527 --> 00:13:17,847
The theory is the criminals they send down there are so dangerous that they've been completely wiped from history.

182
00:13:18,307 --> 00:13:21,867
Now that I think about it, there's a good chance that's where they took your brother.

183
00:13:22,587 --> 00:13:26,167
But the furthest I can take you is level four, so you're on your own after that.

184
00:13:26,167 --> 00:13:27,387
Thanks, Buggy.

185
00:13:27,547 --> 00:13:29,867
I thought you were a real jerk, but I guess I was wrong.

186
00:13:29,967 --> 00:13:30,887
Ha ha ha ha ha!

187
00:13:31,227 --> 00:13:32,207
A deal's a deal.

188
00:13:32,387 --> 00:13:36,487
And if that arm that leads me to Captain John's treasure, I'm getting a real bargain, kid!

189
00:13:36,627 --> 00:13:37,267
Oh!

190
00:13:37,267 --> 00:13:43,447
I shouldn't have opened my big mouth!

191
00:13:44,107 --> 00:13:45,127
Hey, you know what?

192
00:13:45,727 --> 00:13:46,127
What?

193
00:13:47,127 --> 00:13:49,507
If you got caught, you're a pretty crappy pirate.

194
00:13:49,567 --> 00:13:50,407
What the hell, man?

195
00:13:50,467 --> 00:13:51,327
Give me a break!

196
00:13:52,407 --> 00:13:54,267
The idiot didn't even hear me.

197
00:13:54,547 --> 00:13:56,187
I'm lucky he's so stupid.

198
00:13:56,427 --> 00:13:57,087
That's awesome!

199
00:13:57,387 --> 00:13:58,567
This is a treasure map?

200
00:13:58,887 --> 00:13:59,927
I didn't have a clue.

201
00:14:00,407 --> 00:14:01,727
Bet that'll be really fun.

202
00:14:01,727 --> 00:14:09,047
Sorry, kid, but if you know the truth, I'll have to kill you.

203
00:14:10,387 --> 00:14:12,967
You better take this now in case I forget later.

204
00:14:18,027 --> 00:14:22,107
You know that's a treasure map, and you're still going to give it to me?

205
00:14:22,447 --> 00:14:23,307
Yeah, of course.

206
00:14:23,527 --> 00:14:25,607
Treasure's cool and all, but Ace is more important.

207
00:14:25,607 --> 00:14:30,627
But if you give it to me now, what's to stop me from running off with it and leaving you down here to die?

208
00:14:30,707 --> 00:14:31,647
Nothing, I guess.

209
00:14:31,787 --> 00:14:34,567
But you gave your word you'd help out, and that's good enough for me.

210
00:14:34,827 --> 00:14:35,347
Ha ha!

211
00:14:36,767 --> 00:14:40,387
Those trusty eyes, pouring into my soul!

212
00:14:41,087 --> 00:14:44,067
I'm a scoundrel straw hat, can't you see?

213
00:14:44,687 --> 00:14:45,707
Don't do it!

214
00:14:46,047 --> 00:14:47,687
You deserve better than this!

215
00:14:48,107 --> 00:14:49,927
I'm no good for you!

216
00:14:49,927 --> 00:14:59,107
After all this time, I finally have the key to Captain John's secrets, and I owe it all to you!

217
00:14:59,607 --> 00:15:00,347
Thanks, buddy.

218
00:15:00,707 --> 00:15:02,227
You're a real champ!

219
00:15:04,887 --> 00:15:08,147
Now how do I ditch you and get the hell out of here?

220
00:15:08,147 --> 00:15:10,147
Ha ha ha!

221
00:15:10,147 --> 00:15:11,147
Ha ha ha!

222
00:15:13,487 --> 00:15:16,147
Oh, if we break through the walls here, is it like a shortcut?

223
00:15:16,487 --> 00:15:17,267
I can do that!

224
00:15:17,707 --> 00:15:19,027
What's wrong with you?

225
00:15:19,027 --> 00:15:23,487
No!

226
00:15:27,267 --> 00:15:27,767
All right.

227
00:15:28,507 --> 00:15:37,567
We'll be right back.

228
00:15:37,827 --> 00:15:38,587
Bye.

229
00:15:38,647 --> 00:15:39,647
Bye.

230
00:15:39,987 --> 00:15:40,667
Bye.

231
00:15:40,667 --> 00:15:41,107
Bye.

232
00:15:41,267 --> 00:15:41,567
Bye.

233
00:15:42,567 --> 00:15:42,707
Bye.

234
00:15:43,427 --> 00:15:43,707
Bye.

235
00:15:43,867 --> 00:15:44,307
Bye.

236
00:15:44,567 --> 00:15:45,767
Bye.

237
00:15:47,487 --> 00:15:48,047
Bye.

238
00:15:48,087 --> 00:15:48,667
Bye.

239
00:15:49,027 --> 00:15:59,507
I do hope Luffy is safe. I warned him to stay out of trouble, but that may have been in vain.

240
00:16:00,227 --> 00:16:06,427
Breaking your brother out will be challenging enough, but if you get captured as well, who knows what horrors you might face.

241
00:16:06,987 --> 00:16:09,827
One wrong step and you may never see the light of day again.

242
00:16:11,047 --> 00:16:17,007
I know you want to save Ace, but this is dangerous. Please, take care of yourself, too.

243
00:16:17,007 --> 00:16:23,247
I won't let you down. You have my word. Thanks for everything, Hancock. You're the best.

244
00:16:23,747 --> 00:16:26,807
Hancock. Hancock. Hancock.

245
00:16:27,087 --> 00:16:32,927
Oh, my love. I can hear your angelic voice echoing through the chambers of my heart.

246
00:16:34,267 --> 00:16:36,847
Okie dokie. Almost there.

247
00:16:41,427 --> 00:16:44,427
Ooh, that was a good one, wasn't it?

248
00:16:44,427 --> 00:16:47,147
Our jailers are certainly skilled at what they do.

249
00:16:47,707 --> 00:16:55,287
